ica comparison  for a very simple reason  Battlestar Galactica worked because it  took the core principles of the original  show the core of what that show was and  it made something new from it so in this  example then we have to think about what  is the core of Babylon five and then  what could JMS use to create an entirely  new show from so for me there are a  couple of really important bits to it  there was the earth membari War I think  that is really key to this it was not  necessarily the war itself but how Earth  reacted to it he is behind me you are in  front of me you value your lives be  somewhere else so we found out that we  were not alone in the universe and we  started to expand and to explore  we came across the membari and a  conflict started  now that was a conflict that we got  soundly beaten during they were on the  brink of wiping us out  now they chose to surrender when they  found out about the whole Souls thing  I also love to prepare how that conflict  started with JMS and but that wouldn't  really be key to me he could think of  something new fat if he wanted to but  the whole way of them they have their  weapon doors open to show this is our  strength but we come in peace and that  scared the human so we fired first we  thought they were threatening us  I liked that story arc and I kind of  hope he can do something similar but  obviously we'll try and do it in a  different way  that was key though it was not like I  say the war necessarily but the defeat  that was important and the way we then  reacted to it and our reaction was to  build the Babylon stations Babylon 5  being the final one a five mile long  space station in neutral space I think  though also not just the fact that the  station was there but it was an  imperfect station you know we had things  like brown sector we had Wanderers  entrepreneurs and diplomats and Hustlers  coming in and out of the station it was  really a hub for aliens to intermix with  each other the good and the bad now  remembering Babylon 5 was considered the  poor man Star Trek back in the day and  it was never very fair example but it  did run roughly at the same time as the  Next Generation the next generation was  all shiny and everything was great and  there's no money and people were perfect  and you know nobody had a dark side  then we have Babylon 5. what actually  did show the underbelly and the reality  of not just humans but of aliens and  life around the universe them in barring  yes were religious anything but even  they have their dark side  a lot of the other alien species were  more like us than we'd like to admit  we then had the shadow War and the  shadow conflict  now  for me the shadow war was the best part  of Babylon 5. it was the third series I  think was the was the best series  um it showed some of the best um amazing  battle scenes and things but the story  was really sharp  um it just it really it for me that was  my favorite part about five is what made  Babylon 5. if you've never watched  Babylon 5 before to be fair you could  just go back and watch the third series  and you'll be absolutely I think it did  after the shadow War sort of meander a  little bit and never quite got back to  that height  even though some of the conflict where  Sheridan had to go and retake Earth and  all that sort of thing was brilliant it  didn't quite have the same punch as the  shadow conflict  so is the shadow war and that whole  thing core to Babylon 5 do they need to  repeat that in the reboot  I'm not sure they do I think the whole  thing between them in Bari and the Earth  Force battle that is key that needs to  be repeated because that is core to why  the Babylon station was then built we  then need to see The Babylon 5 station  or a new modern version of that we then  need to see obviously the aliens coming  together and that's the whole point of  the show  beyond that I think JMS could really do  whatever the hell he wanted  um obviously there has to be some sort  of conflict Susan Ivanova said it best  here the Babylon project was our last  best Hope For Peace but then in the year  of the Shadow War it became something  greater  our last best hope  for victory  the last best hope for survival of  everybody  now  this could mean a new villain we don't  have to necessarily see the Shadows  return even though God I really hope so  they had some of the best Starship  designs I mean the shadows of it oh man  I really want to see that return because  they're iconic but at the same time  James can't really do that again because  we know that story We Know How It Ends  it's got to do something completely  different  now what he has said about his reboot is  that he has seen what lots of other TV  shows have done before him he has  learned himself over many years of  working in the industry  and he has decided that what he wants to  do is is if Babylon 5 never existed if  he had that story today what would he do  him out so that moves me into one of the  other big areas of some of the comments  I saw don't make it go woke a lot of  people do seem to be very nervous that  this show is just going to be another  mess they don't particularly like most  of new Trek I think apart from strange  new worlds new Trek has been a bit of a  failure for me anyway I just don't like  Discovery I wish I did I tried so hard  um but a lot of people do keep using  this word woke now if you are a regular  sidetracker you'll know that I'm not a  fan of that word I do think that there  is a genuine problem with some  filmmakers and that the word woke is  used to describe but Babylon 5 was kind  of a bit woke in the in you know even 25  years ago he did have a lot of  storylines that would be considered now  to be woke you know he did talk about a  lot of very spiritual matters for a  start and religion as well JMS is really  not afraid to explore the issues of the  time he explored not just the good side  of man but the dark side and I thin